Changelog: 15-11-2026 20:10:01

Added. Console Helpers comes with the portal, as Board Test does: the portal installs it with itself (bundled in the
release, from apps/helpers in a checkout), records it, lists no Uninstall for it and removes it with its own
uninstall. Each helper is a tile of its own on Utilities, from the new [[apps.<key>.helpers]] tables of apps.toml;
a helper that changes the board says so on its tile and asks before it opens, and Reinstall or Update on any of
them installs the app. apps.toml may now mark more than one app required; board stays the first.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 12:45:47

Added. install.sh removes the downloaded portal tarball once it has installed from it, and the SHA256SUMS beside
it when that file lists the tarball (another download's SHA256SUMS stays); the unpacked folder stays. It keeps
build.sha256 in that folder too, so running install.sh from it again still records the build. This covers the
install steps, the portal's own update and check-release.sh. The portal's installer test covers it.

