Changelog: 15-11-2026 03:22:26

Added. install.sh --uninstall removes the whole suite (owner, 15-11-2026): it asks about each other installed app (y
uninstalls it, s keeps it, c cancels before anything is removed), removes Bazzite Test with its own installer (with
--purge, its settings too) and the suite's venv when no app uses it any more. --uninstall --all removes every app
after one confirmation, with --purge their settings as well. Without --purge only the records and releases of the
apps that stay are kept, with the wallpaper. Before, the portal alone went and Bazzite Test and the apps stayed. On
a computer where nothing of the suite is installed it says so and stops.

Changelog: 14-11-2026 18:22:54

Release 1.4.0.

Changelog: 14-11-2026 17:13:40

Added. The portal plays background music (owner, 14-11-2026): a track that plays quietly, over and over, while the
portal is in front. It is the owner's remix of DAT Station's Sea Breeze, made in Audacity. Two new pills on the
Settings page: Music (Yes or No) switches it, apart from Sound, so either can be off while the other is on; Music
track chooses a track of your own (an Ogg, Opus, MP3, FLAC, WAV or M4A file, kept as a copy in the portal's state
folder) or the portal's again. The music waits while the intro or the Portal Tour plays, while the portal is
minimized and while another window has the focus (a game, an app), and plays on from where it was. Without an audio
output the portal plays none. The wiki's Portal page says so, and the Portal Tour is recorded again and shows the
Music pill. The tools that draw the portal (tools/portal_tour.py, tools/portal_screenshot.py) play no music.

